wset (0.2.1-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * r rate changes only the values given: it no longer fills in xset's
    660 ms and 25 a second, needs a delay, and keeps the rate when none is
    given.

 -- Komiljon Sobitov <komiljon.sobitov.uzb@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:19:43 +0500

wset (0.2.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * r rate works like xset's: 660 and 25 for missing values, an interval of
    1000 / rate, and it turns auto-repeat on.
  * GNOME: r, r on/off and q no longer need a Wayland connection, so wset
    also works in a GNOME X11 session; check that GSettings kept the values.
  * Sway: set every keyboard, including those with their own input block,
    and check that sway took the values.
  * q prints the lines xset q uses; take -q, --help and --version.

 -- Komiljon Sobitov <komiljon.sobitov.uzb@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0500

